WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:05.150
Leone, stop! We don't have time 
for something so unimportant!

00:05.150 --> 00:09.860
Unimportant? There's nothing 
more important to me right now!

00:12.540 --> 00:14.520
I see. You've grown.

00:14.840 --> 00:15.980
I won't let you get away!

00:19.160 --> 00:20.240
Leone!

00:21.810 --> 00:23.080
Don't move.

00:23.080 --> 00:25.550
I'd prefer you stay out of this.

00:25.550 --> 00:30.010
We don't want to hurt the 
daughter of the Arcia family.

00:30.010 --> 00:32.790
My father may be the Chancellor,

00:32.790 --> 00:36.970
but I'm only an academy student, 
and yet they know who I am...

00:37.510 --> 00:40.980
Just who are the Bloodchain Brigade?

00:56.110 --> 00:59.070
<b><u>Reborn</u></b>

00:56.110 --> 00:59.070
<b>to Master the Blade
\h\h\h\h\hFrom Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire\h\h\h\h\h</b>

00:56.110 --> 00:59.070
<b>to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire</b>

02:12.060 --> 02:15.900
<b>Episode 10    The Plan to Attack a Highlander</b>

02:15.910 --> 02:18.990
Mother and Father are gone!

02:18.990 --> 02:22.770
But for the people of Almen 
who were left behind...

02:22.770 --> 02:26.780
I can never forgive you!

02:26.780 --> 02:32.240
And if you lose Almen, 
you'll have nothing else left!

02:34.460 --> 02:38.770
The royal court has decided to offer up 
Almen to the Hierarch Highlanders

02:38.770 --> 02:43.180
to restore relations with them.

02:43.180 --> 02:45.640
But why would they do that?

02:45.640 --> 02:49.810
It's outlived its purpose as a place from 
which to monitor the frozen Prismer.

02:50.630 --> 02:53.660
I suppose they feel they have 
nothing to lose by offering it up.

02:53.660 --> 02:55.590
That's not right, though!

02:55.590 --> 02:58.250
Where's the justice in that?

02:59.230 --> 03:03.650
If you must rage against someone, 
direct your ire toward your foolish king

03:03.650 --> 03:07.210
who'd hand over his own people 
to curry favor with Highlanders.

03:07.210 --> 03:10.280
The Hyral Menas will be 
handed over in four days.

03:10.280 --> 03:12.980
The Highlander emissary will come by boat.

03:14.130 --> 03:17.240
We'll attack and kill the 
emissary when they arrive.

03:17.240 --> 03:21.090
Our only enemies are the Highlanders, who 
are trying to steal the very land from us.

03:21.090 --> 03:23.890
You're telling us your plan?

03:24.470 --> 03:27.060
What are you plotting?

03:27.060 --> 03:29.740
If you'd like to try something of your own,

03:29.740 --> 03:33.020
feel free to take advantage 
of the chaos we'll cause.

03:33.020 --> 03:36.230
But don't get in our way.

03:36.230 --> 03:38.490
And you think we'll just believe you?

03:38.810 --> 03:41.220
That's up to you.

03:41.220 --> 03:42.960
Now, goodbye.

03:42.960 --> 03:43.860
Brother!

03:46.680 --> 03:50.080
But I... No matter what your reason is...

03:50.080 --> 03:52.870
Do what you think is best.

03:52.870 --> 03:55.110
Nobody will stop you.

03:56.060 --> 03:58.200
But... You've grown.

03:58.630 --> 04:00.810
I can't do a thing for you,

04:01.300 --> 04:02.550
but that makes me happy.

04:03.180 --> 04:04.730
Keep it up.

04:10.220 --> 04:11.250
Leone...

04:11.930 --> 04:14.770
We need to head back and tell everyone.

04:16.700 --> 04:22.730
So you're saying that if we don't stop them, 
the Highland will take Ripple?

04:22.730 --> 04:25.580
And the town of Almen, to boot!

04:25.580 --> 04:28.160
That's just not right!

04:28.480 --> 04:31.110
Yes. We have to do something.

04:31.110 --> 04:33.220
But what?

04:33.750 --> 04:35.970
I have a plan.

04:37.190 --> 04:39.530
I see.

04:39.530 --> 04:41.490
That would work!

04:41.490 --> 04:43.270
But it's too reckless!

04:43.270 --> 04:47.770
Every time Chris says something, 
it's either reckless or insane.

04:47.770 --> 04:49.240
Yeah...

04:49.240 --> 04:50.780
Agreed.

04:52.980 --> 04:56.190
In a sense, they trust you, Inglis.

04:57.390 --> 05:00.750
We'll go with Inglis's idea, then.

05:00.750 --> 05:03.370
I'll get things started on my end first!

05:03.360 --> 05:05.820
<b>Four Days Later</b>

05:08.640 --> 05:10.540
Wh-What is this?

05:10.540 --> 05:14.450
What do you mean? 
They're maid outfits, of course.

05:14.450 --> 05:20.260
They're going to infiltrate the court 
under the guise of part-time servants.

05:20.260 --> 05:21.840
These maid outfits are great, huh?

05:21.840 --> 05:22.650
Yup!

05:23.200 --> 05:27.520
Principal Miliera, 
was there really no better way?

05:27.520 --> 05:31.300
I thought it was a great idea!

05:31.300 --> 05:34.840
One that takes full advantage 
of their cuteness!

05:35.190 --> 05:37.790
It'll be okay, Silva!

05:37.790 --> 05:41.740
When the Bloodchain Brigade 
comes to attack, we'll defeat them!

05:42.150 --> 05:45.730
While protecting the king 
and the Highlander emissary.

05:45.730 --> 05:47.220
Don't forget that.

05:47.600 --> 05:49.090
Okay!

05:49.090 --> 05:50.570
Good grief...

05:51.530 --> 05:54.540
When are they handing over Ripple?

05:54.850 --> 05:58.850
Right after the ceremony at the court.

05:58.850 --> 06:03.470
We wanted a little more time, 
but the royal guards weren't having it.

06:03.470 --> 06:08.120
But at the start they were saying, 
"Hand her over immediately!"

06:08.120 --> 06:09.830
This is a major victory!

06:09.830 --> 06:12.510
All thanks to Silva.

06:12.510 --> 06:14.780
I have a brother in the Royal Guard.

06:14.780 --> 06:18.470
I wasn't sure about going to him for help, 
but it didn't feel like we had a choice.

06:18.870 --> 06:22.870
While the royal guards are 
busy protecting the court,

06:22.870 --> 06:26.370
Silva and I will feed Ripple our mana, 
making her summon magicite beasts

06:26.370 --> 06:28.720
until there aren't any more left to summon.

06:28.720 --> 06:34.330
Then there'll be no reason 
to take her back to the Highland.

06:34.330 --> 06:36.340
It's a little crazy, but it'll work!

06:36.340 --> 06:38.310
It's not a little crazy. It's insane.

06:38.960 --> 06:41.140
But we don't have a choice.

06:41.850 --> 06:44.790
I'll be counting on you two. 
For Ripple's sake, too.

06:46.650 --> 06:48.450
Wh-What?

06:48.450 --> 06:52.590
Silva, do you like Ripple?

06:53.650 --> 06:55.230
Don't be ridiculous!

06:55.720 --> 06:57.380
Oh, my...

06:57.380 --> 07:00.020
You don't have to hide it!

07:00.020 --> 07:04.100
I do not! It would be most improper 
to think of a Hyral Menas that way.

07:04.690 --> 07:07.490
I do respect her deeply...

07:07.490 --> 07:09.910
Respect?

07:09.910 --> 07:12.660
When I was young, she saved my life.

07:13.370 --> 07:17.280
There was a sudden rain 
of Prism Flow one day.

07:17.280 --> 07:19.580
A friend and I were attacked 
by a magicite beast.

07:20.460 --> 07:24.580
We both ran... and he died protecting me.

07:25.300 --> 07:29.750
I was weak, and so he, 
a Runeless, had to die.

07:31.030 --> 07:35.430
Just as I thought it was all over, 
Ripple saved me.

07:41.360 --> 07:44.120
She held me as I cried, and she said...

07:44.740 --> 07:46.250
Get stronger.

07:46.250 --> 07:48.850
For the sake of your friend 
who protected you.

07:48.850 --> 07:53.720
And so you can protect dozens—
no, hundreds of times as many people more.

07:55.190 --> 07:58.190
Those words are what made me who I am today.

07:58.590 --> 08:04.010
I trained hard every day, so that I 
could be someone who protects others.

08:04.490 --> 08:07.580
<i>So he didn't hate the Runeless after all.</i>

08:07.580 --> 08:12.560
<i>He wanted to keep them from danger, and he 
was willing to sacrifice his own life for it.</i>

08:13.390 --> 08:18.120
I'm sorry for making you 
remember something like that.

08:18.120 --> 08:20.790
It was a long time ago. 
Don't worry about it.

08:20.790 --> 08:24.430
Is the reason you use a gun Artifact...

08:24.820 --> 08:29.920
Yes. I thought it would make it 
easier to fight alongside Ripple.

08:30.510 --> 08:32.370
That's wonderful...

08:32.370 --> 08:34.870
I'm sure Ripple will be very happy.

08:35.160 --> 08:39.530
Ripple remembered Silva.

08:40.090 --> 08:44.320
She looked upset... I don't know why.

08:44.930 --> 08:49.290
No, it's probably because I'm not 
strong enough for her to rely on me.

08:49.290 --> 08:50.610
That's not...

08:50.610 --> 08:53.430
Either way, we need to carry out the plan.

08:54.050 --> 08:56.890
I don't want Ripple to be taken 
from our country yet.

08:57.270 --> 09:00.800
Yes. And that's why we need 
to do our best tomorrow!

09:00.800 --> 09:03.980
Leave it to us, Silva!

09:03.980 --> 09:06.500
Right. I'll do my best on my end, too.

09:06.930 --> 09:12.940
No, I'd like to meet up with you guys 
and join the fight, so take your time.

09:14.950 --> 09:17.350
Just how obsessed
are you with fighting?

09:21.080 --> 09:24.660
New girls! Come help over here!

09:24.980 --> 09:26.180
Okay!

09:26.960 --> 09:28.710
It looks great!

09:28.710 --> 09:31.090
The food at the court's 
really something else.

09:31.410 --> 09:34.350
Rani, you ate too much. 
There's no shrimp left.

09:34.350 --> 09:37.530
And just how much meat 
are <i>you</i> going to eat, Chris?

09:39.090 --> 09:42.370
I'm eating a little from everything 
so they don't find out!

09:43.260 --> 09:45.600
It's a waste, too!

09:45.600 --> 09:49.710
When the Bloodchain Brigade comes, 
nobody's going to get to eat this food.

09:54.690 --> 09:57.240
Nobody can know about the attack.

09:57.240 --> 10:01.260
We don't want to talk about it and have 
them think we're co-conspirators.

10:01.650 --> 10:04.290
You say that, but you're 
just trying to make sure

10:04.290 --> 10:07.510
you've got as many enemies 
to fight as possible, right?

10:07.510 --> 10:08.990
That's right.

10:08.990 --> 10:10.340
Chris...

10:11.120 --> 10:15.240
Well, whatever. Until that 
time comes, we have to work!

10:16.630 --> 10:19.980
Oh, the king has arrived!

10:20.300 --> 10:21.900
King Carius!

10:21.900 --> 10:24.120
Hail to the king!

10:24.120 --> 10:28.470
Your Majesty! Your Majesty, King Carius!

10:28.470 --> 10:31.930
The king's got a Special-class rune, huh?

10:32.310 --> 10:35.380
He must be strong. 
It'll be easy to protect him.

10:35.380 --> 10:37.050
We don't know that for sure.

10:38.150 --> 10:42.910
<i>If you're doing your job as king, 
you won't have any time left to practice.</i>

10:43.240 --> 10:44.750
<i>I know that firsthand.</i>

10:45.980 --> 10:50.340
Today, I'm pleased to welcome 
an emissary from the Highland.

10:50.840 --> 10:54.620
They've promised to send a new Hyral Menas,

10:54.620 --> 10:58.040
who will lead our kingdom 
to even greater glory.

10:58.040 --> 11:00.830
What about Almen?

11:00.830 --> 11:03.740
Maybe they don't have to 
hand it over anymore.

11:03.740 --> 11:09.170
That's not it. At times like these, 
you just say the good things, not the bad.

11:09.170 --> 11:11.030
That's kind of sneaky!

11:11.590 --> 11:14.120
Now, let us welcome the emissary.

11:15.240 --> 11:17.850
Everyone, be on your best behavior.

11:17.850 --> 11:18.540
Yes, sire.

11:20.400 --> 11:22.990
<b>Highlander Arch Lord
(Great General) Ivel</b>

11:22.990 --> 11:25.720
Wow, he's cute!

11:25.720 --> 11:28.020
His eyes and hair are such pretty colors.

11:28.020 --> 11:29.070
Yeah.

11:29.290 --> 11:33.800
Allow me to introduce you all. 
This is the Highlander emissary, Lord Ivel.

11:34.080 --> 11:37.710
Despite his young age, 
he is already a great general.

11:37.710 --> 11:39.730
Oh, is that true?

11:39.730 --> 11:43.510
Then he must be of a higher rank 
than a typical emissary.

11:43.510 --> 11:48.880
Emissaries who get sent to the surface 
are just low-level foreign officers.

11:48.880 --> 11:53.220
I bear the rank of Arch Lord 
and command the Chief Hierarch's armies.

11:51.340 --> 11:54.250
I take it all back. He's not cute at all!

11:53.220 --> 11:55.320
I'm nothing like them.

11:54.250 --> 11:55.310
True.

11:55.310 --> 11:56.760
Wonderful!

11:56.760 --> 11:58.640
It's an honor to see him!

11:58.640 --> 12:01.290
This is a day I'll remember forever!

11:59.550 --> 12:01.440
I don't like this.

12:01.440 --> 12:04.730
Everybody sucking up 
to that mean little kid.

12:04.730 --> 12:06.170
Yeah.

12:06.170 --> 12:09.340
Hey, Chris! Pay attention!

12:13.550 --> 12:15.470
This is hilarious!

12:15.470 --> 12:21.020
We get a whole city just for swapping out 
one defective Hyral Menas!

12:21.250 --> 12:24.750
You're losing the lives of your fellow men, 
you're losing a valuable asset,

12:24.750 --> 12:27.760
and you're still trying to suck up to me!

12:27.760 --> 12:28.960
You're all crazy.

12:29.950 --> 12:34.460
You fools don't realize that 
any one of you could be next.

12:30.170 --> 12:33.560
I hate to say it, but he's right.

12:33.560 --> 12:34.810
Yup.

12:34.810 --> 12:40.050
Well, for my part, 
it's easier to deal with fools.

12:40.050 --> 12:42.910
Thanks. For being so stupid.

12:45.730 --> 12:48.500
There's no need to thank us, Lord Ivel.

12:48.500 --> 12:51.950
We are fools, as you say.

12:51.950 --> 12:54.730
And I, as king, am the 
greatest fool of them all.

12:54.730 --> 13:00.340
I only hope that you will teach us 
to be as smart as you.

13:01.270 --> 13:02.990
Please teach us...

13:04.310 --> 13:07.820
I don't want to see this. It's pathetic.

13:07.820 --> 13:10.760
Yeah? It's kinda interesting, though.

13:11.330 --> 13:14.260
<i>Normally, one would respond 
to such provocations with anger.</i>

13:14.260 --> 13:15.700
<i>For him to react this way...</i>

13:15.700 --> 13:20.350
<i>Either he's not human, or he has 
something he truly believes in.</i>

13:20.700 --> 13:24.410
You're interesting, for a fool.

13:26.380 --> 13:28.030
Magicite beasts!

13:29.240 --> 13:30.520
They're here!

13:30.790 --> 13:32.430
Let's do it, Chris!

13:32.430 --> 13:34.220
Huh?

13:47.840 --> 13:49.590
Who is that girl?

13:49.590 --> 13:53.300
I'm a maid, so it's my job 
to clean up the banquet hall!

13:53.720 --> 13:55.180
Rani, you take—

13:57.890 --> 13:59.260
What was that?

14:00.200 --> 14:02.930
<i>I've never seen that attack before.</i>

14:02.930 --> 14:06.120
Seal the exits! Prepare for 
an attack from the windows!

14:06.390 --> 14:09.570
Protect the king and the emissary!

14:09.570 --> 14:10.440
Yes, sir!

14:13.940 --> 14:15.630
How obnoxious.

14:17.340 --> 14:20.110
Die!

14:23.830 --> 14:25.140
I can't move...

14:25.140 --> 14:26.860
L-Let me go!

14:26.860 --> 14:27.840
No.

14:27.840 --> 14:31.810
The Highlanders must be stopped 
before they take all our homes!

14:30.850 --> 14:33.510
Is he with the Bloodchain Brigade?

14:33.510 --> 14:36.350
Hey. Nobody asked for your help.

14:36.350 --> 14:39.700
Did you think a weakling like him 
could so much as scratch me?

14:39.700 --> 14:41.600
My apologies.

14:42.000 --> 14:43.540
Well, it's fine.

14:43.540 --> 14:45.580
Restrain him.

14:46.390 --> 14:48.320
<i>The same light as before...</i>

15:06.350 --> 15:07.920
Chris, are you okay?!

15:08.190 --> 15:09.990
Y-Yeah.

15:09.990 --> 15:12.060
Not much scares you, huh?

15:12.060 --> 15:13.300
Thanks.

15:13.300 --> 15:16.530
Did you do that deliberately? 
That's disgusting!

15:16.530 --> 15:21.030
Yeah? If anything's disgusting, 
it's inviting someone to a banquet

15:21.030 --> 15:23.720
and then trying to kill them.

15:24.060 --> 15:28.900
N-No! I assure you, 
our country was not behind this!

15:28.900 --> 15:30.330
It was the Bloodchain Brigade,

15:30.330 --> 15:33.380
a group of rebels that have been 
active in our lands lately...

15:34.480 --> 15:38.310
I'm willing to believe that, 
but that's still a problem.

15:38.310 --> 15:39.700
A problem?

15:39.700 --> 15:45.170
Your incompetence put a 
Highlander emissary in danger.

15:45.650 --> 15:48.870
How do you intend to atone for that sin?

15:49.860 --> 15:52.460
Please, show mercy!

15:52.740 --> 15:56.810
I, Carius, am prepared 
to accept any punishment!

15:56.810 --> 15:58.850
Your Majesty!

15:58.850 --> 16:01.260
No, that's not good enough.

16:01.890 --> 16:06.970
An apology only means something 
when it's between two equals.

16:07.400 --> 16:09.950
But the Highland and 
the surface aren't equal.

16:10.550 --> 16:13.790
You're just the boss of 
a group of cattle we keep.

16:13.790 --> 16:16.780
And an apology from cattle 
means nothing.

16:17.460 --> 16:18.650
So...

16:25.970 --> 16:29.210
I'm taking an arm.

16:29.210 --> 16:31.220
Y-Your Majesty!

16:31.220 --> 16:32.440
Damn you!

16:32.440 --> 16:34.550
Even if you're the Highland emissary...

16:34.830 --> 16:37.290
Calm yourselves, everyone!

16:37.290 --> 16:42.250
Anyone who harms the emissary will 
be executed in the name of the king!

16:42.250 --> 16:44.340
Y-Yes, sire...

16:44.950 --> 16:49.700
Thank you for your mercy, Lord Ivel.

16:49.930 --> 16:50.780
Your Majesty...

16:50.780 --> 16:54.490
Chris, is this really okay?

16:54.490 --> 16:56.190
Is this really right?

16:56.190 --> 16:57.380
It's not...

16:57.380 --> 16:59.030
That's up to the individual, isn't it?

16:59.340 --> 17:02.240
What you think is right, is right.

17:02.740 --> 17:04.810
<i>Everyone really does have their own ideas.</i>

17:04.810 --> 17:08.580
<i>Some pledge loyalty to the Highlanders, 
to keep their people alive.</i>

17:09.150 --> 17:13.160
<i>Others try to become stronger, 
to become equals to the Highlanders.</i>

17:13.480 --> 17:16.640
<i>What will come of the contrast between them?</i>

17:16.640 --> 17:20.380
<i>Well, that's for the people 
of this era to decide.</i>

17:20.950 --> 17:23.980
Anyway, Rani, we have something 
we have to hurry and do.

17:28.350 --> 17:29.640
Excuse me.

17:32.290 --> 17:34.280
We'll try to heal your wound.

17:34.280 --> 17:35.100
Rani.

17:36.240 --> 17:37.520
I'll give it a shot.

17:44.390 --> 17:45.700
It's healing!

17:46.310 --> 17:49.730
<i>This is more difficult 
than what she did for Silva...</i>

17:51.520 --> 17:54.250
<i>Rani works hard.</i>

17:54.630 --> 17:57.140
Hey, what are you doing?

17:57.140 --> 17:58.910
We are healing him.

17:58.910 --> 18:00.830
May we continue?

18:00.830 --> 18:02.860
I don't mind.

18:02.860 --> 18:04.230
Thank you.

18:04.230 --> 18:10.070
But I'm going to take someone 
else's arm instead.

18:10.070 --> 18:16.020
Now, who's going to offer up 
their arm to make me happy?

18:17.140 --> 18:19.000
If my healing comes at 
such a cost, I cannot...

18:19.490 --> 18:22.940
Try and take my arm, then!

18:23.180 --> 18:27.160
<i>It'll give me a chance to see 
that power up close.</i>

18:27.160 --> 18:28.610
Sure.

18:28.610 --> 18:31.630
Normally, I wouldn't care 
about the arm of a Runeless,

18:32.120 --> 18:35.960
but I can't wait to see that smile 
on your face turn to a scream.

18:35.960 --> 18:37.990
C-Chris!

18:37.990 --> 18:39.840
It's fine, Rani.

18:39.840 --> 18:41.670
Just keep healing His Majesty.

18:41.670 --> 18:45.360
I look forward to hearing 
how you'll shriek in pain.

18:46.150 --> 18:49.500
Yeah, it's not just mana moving.

18:49.500 --> 18:51.850
It's a bunch of different 
wavelengths mixed together.

18:51.850 --> 18:53.680
You don't know anything!

18:53.680 --> 18:55.200
Now, here I go!

18:55.200 --> 18:58.130
I won't stop, no matter how much you cry!

19:00.490 --> 19:01.550
What?

19:02.570 --> 19:05.650
H-Hey, that was the same 
thing he did before, right?

19:03.480 --> 19:06.400
<i>I'd turned down its power 
so he couldn't sense it,</i>

19:05.650 --> 19:07.670
Y-Yeah, but...

19:06.400 --> 19:09.330
<i>but I definitely activated 
an Aether Shell just now!</i>

19:09.330 --> 19:11.770
<i>And his power exceeded even that...</i>

19:12.250 --> 19:15.350
<i>I like this maid outfit, 
so I'm sorry to see it damaged,</i>

19:15.350 --> 19:17.230
<i>but that was a most impressive display!</i>

19:17.620 --> 19:20.440
Amazing! That was amazing!

19:20.440 --> 19:22.810
D-Damn you!

19:27.820 --> 19:31.320
Maybe it's not that powerful after all?

19:31.320 --> 19:34.820
But it definitely killed the 
assassin and took the king's arm!

19:35.200 --> 19:38.140
I see! It's not just mana.

19:38.140 --> 19:42.020
It's similar, but using 
something more powerful!

19:42.670 --> 19:44.480
It's Mana Refinement!

19:44.480 --> 19:46.620
It increases the purity 
and efficiency of mana!

19:47.080 --> 19:50.250
You surface dwellers shouldn't 
be able to defend against it!

19:50.250 --> 19:51.560
But you...

19:51.560 --> 19:54.510
Quality over quantity, right?

19:54.510 --> 19:58.640
If it evolves along that path, 
it might catch up to aether someday!

19:58.640 --> 19:59.970
Wonderful!

20:00.530 --> 20:03.730
I can't understand your power at all...

20:03.730 --> 20:07.340
What is that power? Who are you?

20:07.760 --> 20:08.930
Who the hell are you?!

20:12.320 --> 20:14.120
Just a maid. Why?

20:14.560 --> 20:16.490
Damn you...

20:16.490 --> 20:18.400
Don't you <i>dare</i> mock me!

20:21.270 --> 20:23.740
Why? It's not working at all!

20:24.670 --> 20:26.370
Even if you're a child,

20:26.370 --> 20:30.040
I don't think it's a good idea to keep 
touching a girl's breasts like that.

20:30.530 --> 20:32.270
Oh, sorry.

20:33.980 --> 20:35.540
Now, continue!

20:35.540 --> 20:38.460
Please, cut off my arm!

20:38.460 --> 20:41.520
Inglis, was it?

20:41.520 --> 20:43.620
You're no maid!

20:43.620 --> 20:47.180
Tell me your true identity! 
What are you planning?!

20:47.180 --> 20:49.210
My true identity?

20:49.210 --> 20:50.600
Actually...

20:50.600 --> 20:55.010
I'm a part-time maid! I wanted money 
to buy lots of yummy food.

20:55.360 --> 20:58.610
So you're not going to answer me?

20:58.610 --> 20:59.600
Then...

20:59.600 --> 21:02.110
At least show me your power!

21:02.110 --> 21:04.610
Come on! Attack me!

21:04.610 --> 21:09.370
But weren't you the one who wanted 
my arm instead of the king's?

21:09.370 --> 21:11.030
Forget that!

21:11.030 --> 21:12.820
Come on! Attack me!

21:12.820 --> 21:17.940
Personally, I'd love nothing more 
than to duel you, but...

21:17.940 --> 21:18.920
Stand down.

21:19.620 --> 21:25.760
Even if it's what he wants, 
you must not harm a Highlander!

21:25.760 --> 21:28.230
You must...

21:29.060 --> 21:31.710
You really are a dumb animal.

21:31.710 --> 21:34.180
There's no point in trying to suck up to me.

21:35.150 --> 21:37.270
The reason that I, an Arch Lord,

21:37.270 --> 21:41.350
came all the way to the surface 
was not to bring you a Hyral Menas

21:41.350 --> 21:43.820
or repair relationships between our nations!

21:44.070 --> 21:46.280
The Chief Hierarch is angry!

21:46.280 --> 21:49.750
One day, this whole country 
will be wiped from the map.

21:50.200 --> 21:53.400
Then why did you come here?

21:53.400 --> 21:54.840
Because...

23:44.980 --> 23:49.980
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

23:44.980 --> 23:49.980
<b>Please go 
home,
 Highlander!</b>

23:44.980 --> 23:49.980
Comic by Kuromura Moto
